WEBVTT

00:10.593 --> 00:14.639
The perpetrator becomes the victim,
and you lose the upper hand.

00:15.140 --> 00:16.808
That's all fabricated!

00:17.308 --> 00:21.062
A sloppy investigation has turned
a living person into a dead one.

00:21.146 --> 00:26.151
And then she vanished,
like she never existed in the first place.

00:26.234 --> 00:27.527
WANTED: FUGITIVE FOR FRAUD

00:27.610 --> 00:29.738
What do you think made her so sure?

00:30.280 --> 00:31.448
The visible evidence?

00:31.531 --> 00:32.490
SUSPECT

00:32.574 --> 00:33.700
The word on the street?

00:34.200 --> 00:35.452
It's the pattern.

00:37.037 --> 00:38.872
The suspect's crimes follow a pattern.

00:39.581 --> 00:42.709
She cons a large sum of money,
fakes her own death,

00:42.792 --> 00:45.128
assumes a new identity,

00:45.962 --> 00:47.797
and sets up an even bigger con.

00:48.298 --> 00:50.759
Did the search warrant include
Boudoir's bank account?

00:51.551 --> 00:53.553
- No, I'll apply now.
- It'll be too late.

00:54.054 --> 00:56.181
There's a way to check without it.
Follow me.

00:58.933 --> 01:01.519
Why did the money come in?
Didn't anyone check?

01:01.603 --> 01:02.604
I'm sorry, ma'am.

01:02.687 --> 01:05.648
Call Violent Crimes.
What the hell are they trying to pull?

01:08.276 --> 01:09.360
What's going on?

01:09.903 --> 01:10.987
"What's going on?"

01:11.613 --> 01:13.281
You said Boudoir was all a scam.

01:13.782 --> 01:15.742
Then how the hell is money coming in?

01:16.367 --> 01:17.952
What money are you talking about?

01:18.036 --> 01:20.371
The 15 billion won
Jeong Yeo-jin embezzled!

01:21.956 --> 01:24.084
The full amount was just paid back.

01:25.668 --> 01:26.503
WITHDRAWAL

01:27.420 --> 01:30.048
I know this is a bullshit ploy
to cover up the case.

01:30.548 --> 01:32.884
Why didn't you even freeze the account?

01:32.967 --> 01:34.844
You were so smug raiding that place.

01:34.928 --> 01:36.930
What, did you take a payoff or something?

01:37.013 --> 01:38.848
- You fucking shit!
- Ma'am, no.

01:38.932 --> 01:40.100
- Let go of me!
- Hold on.

01:40.183 --> 01:41.017
- You!
- No, stop.

01:41.101 --> 01:43.103
Is that how you got promoted, asshole?

01:43.186 --> 01:44.270
We can still catch her.

01:44.354 --> 01:46.481
"Catch"? The suspect is dead.

01:46.564 --> 01:48.108
The suspect is still alive!

01:50.944 --> 01:51.778
What?

01:53.321 --> 01:54.155
Hey.

01:54.656 --> 01:57.575
Looks like our cases are really connected.

01:58.368 --> 02:02.163
I'm about to lose it, too,
so just hand over Boudoir's bank records.

02:05.917 --> 02:08.545
I'm sure you went over them
while tracking Nox's accounts.

02:11.840 --> 02:12.841
Give it to me.

02:16.845 --> 02:19.264
We have less than three days
to hold Jeong in custody.

02:19.347 --> 02:21.224
Get this solved by then, no matter what.

02:22.100 --> 02:24.060
Please authorize a wanted notice.

02:25.436 --> 02:29.107
At this rate, we're practically aiding
the suspect's crime ourselves.

02:31.568 --> 02:33.653
Please help us bring her in responsibly.

02:34.654 --> 02:37.532
Say we issue a public notice. Then what?

02:37.615 --> 02:40.785
The suspect has been meticulously erasing
her tracks up until now.

02:41.286 --> 02:43.329
But she can't erase one thing.

02:43.413 --> 02:44.914
People's memories of her.

02:45.707 --> 02:49.210
There must be someone who remembers her
before she took a new identity.

02:49.711 --> 02:50.712
If we find them…

02:53.006 --> 02:54.924
we can identify the suspect.

02:55.008 --> 02:56.426
That's not enough.

02:56.926 --> 03:02.098
A no-name con artist managed to dupe
high-society figures everyone knows.

03:02.182 --> 03:06.728
If this gets out, the public will track
the suspect down on their own.

03:06.811 --> 03:09.981
It's only a matter of time
before we locate her escape route.

03:12.192 --> 03:13.318
And if we lose her?

03:13.401 --> 03:14.319
She won't last.

03:14.402 --> 03:17.906
In the end,
she'll lose her cool and reveal herself.

03:17.989 --> 03:19.282
That will be our only chance

03:19.365 --> 03:22.869
to question her
about the Jane Doe sewer murder case.

03:22.952 --> 03:24.078
But you just said

03:24.162 --> 03:27.373
you want to do a public search for her
as the Boudoir fraud suspect.

03:27.457 --> 03:30.585
Up to this point,
we were pawns in the suspect's setup.

03:31.294 --> 03:35.048
This time, I'll lure her into mine.

03:35.131 --> 03:37.133
You want to con the con artist?

03:38.593 --> 03:39.677
And the evidence?

03:39.761 --> 03:41.638
All we have so far is circumstantial.

03:41.721 --> 03:43.306
You have nothing?

03:43.806 --> 03:46.643
And you're asking me
to authorize a public search?

03:46.726 --> 03:48.144
The suspect's statement,

03:48.228 --> 03:51.689
no, her presence alone
will be the most conclusive evidence.

03:51.773 --> 03:54.651
I'm positive I can get a confession.

04:15.421 --> 04:16.464
Mark my words.

04:17.423 --> 04:19.550
This could make you or break you.

04:25.848 --> 04:26.683
Thank you, sir.

04:27.183 --> 04:29.811
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY
REGIONAL INVESTIGATION DIVISION

04:32.563 --> 04:35.566
This is Park Mu-gyeong
of the Seoul Violent Crimes Unit.

04:35.650 --> 04:37.443
Over the years, the suspect has changed

04:37.527 --> 04:39.737
her name, age,
nationality, job, and education,

04:39.821 --> 04:42.115
living under
at least three false identities.

04:42.198 --> 04:45.952
Due to the crime's severity,
a public wanted notice has been issued.

04:46.452 --> 04:47.704
Effective immediately.

04:48.329 --> 04:51.958
If anyone knows
or has recently seen the suspect,

04:52.041 --> 04:54.877
please contact
the Seoul Violent Crimes Unit.

04:56.546 --> 04:57.380
What's going on?

04:57.463 --> 04:59.424
We apologize. We retract the notice.

04:59.507 --> 05:02.677
We'll have a press conference
immediately after our investigation…

05:03.177 --> 05:04.095
What are you doing?

05:04.178 --> 05:05.013
Well, you see…

05:05.638 --> 05:08.141
Sarah Kim is here voluntarily.

05:12.020 --> 05:13.187
Why did it have to be

05:14.105 --> 05:15.148
now, of all times?

05:18.943 --> 05:21.029
Did you gather all the evidence
on the list?

05:21.112 --> 05:22.864
- Yes, I got everything here.
- Okay.

05:24.282 --> 05:27.952
Make sure you gather everything.
Don't leave anything out.

05:28.036 --> 05:28.911
Yes, sir.

05:28.995 --> 05:30.413
Do you think she'll confess?

05:30.496 --> 05:32.248
The suspect came voluntarily.

05:32.332 --> 05:34.250
- Everyone focus, okay?
- Yes, sir.

05:34.334 --> 05:35.585
JANE DOE SEWER MURDER REPORT

05:41.883 --> 05:47.138
INTERVIEW RECORDING ROOM 1

05:47.221 --> 05:50.099
Do you know when we find people
who vanish voluntarily?

05:51.517 --> 05:53.102
When they decide to return.

06:28.096 --> 06:30.056
RECORD OF STATEMENT (SUSPECT)

06:30.765 --> 06:32.308
Are you turning yourself in?

06:32.934 --> 06:34.852
No. I voluntarily presented myself.

06:37.855 --> 06:39.399
Let me change the question.

06:40.733 --> 06:41.901
What is your name?

06:42.860 --> 06:44.070
It's Sarah Kim.

06:44.570 --> 06:47.573
There's no record of a Sarah Kim anywhere.

06:48.074 --> 06:50.952
No name, birthplace, age, or education.

06:52.412 --> 06:53.746
Let me ask you again.

06:54.580 --> 06:55.748
What is your name?

06:58.167 --> 07:00.628
I already told you. Sarah Kim.

07:04.841 --> 07:07.009
Would you rather not reveal who you are?

07:08.636 --> 07:11.264
It means who I am is not important.

07:11.973 --> 07:14.767
If you see me as a con artist,
I'm a con artist.

07:15.268 --> 07:17.520
If you see me as a businesswoman,
I am one.

07:18.938 --> 07:21.023
But if you see me just as a person,

07:22.942 --> 07:24.652
then you'd be able to understand me.

07:29.782 --> 07:31.701
What if I can't understand you?

07:35.413 --> 07:37.331
Then you will never know me.

07:40.334 --> 07:42.628
THE ART OF SARAH

07:44.380 --> 07:47.884
BOUDOIR

07:56.476 --> 07:58.102
Feel free to say anything you want.

07:58.603 --> 08:00.480
You can tell me a convincing lie,

08:00.980 --> 08:02.815
as you did to others until now.

08:06.903 --> 08:11.407
You think you know me
when all you've seen is my ankle.

08:12.450 --> 08:14.744
You're the person who created Boudoir.

08:15.745 --> 08:16.579
I am.

08:17.079 --> 08:18.164
I won't deny that.

08:18.664 --> 08:20.541
Are you admitting to the fraud charge?

08:20.625 --> 08:22.210
It wasn't fraud.

08:24.837 --> 08:27.632
I did plan and produce Boudoir completely.

08:28.341 --> 08:31.677
Anyone can make a bag,
but not everyone can build a luxury brand.

08:33.471 --> 08:35.014
I accomplished that.

08:36.182 --> 08:38.017
So why would I deny that?

08:40.311 --> 08:42.647
Everyone's the same
once they're in that seat.

08:42.730 --> 08:44.398
They end up resorting to pathos.

08:44.482 --> 08:46.484
I want to be wealthy for a day
before I die.

08:48.110 --> 08:50.321
A reduced sentence
is her only way to survive.

08:51.113 --> 08:53.699
To me, it wasn't a con.
It was a matter of survival.

08:54.867 --> 08:57.078
The world is kind yet indifferent.

08:58.955 --> 09:01.249
On one side,
a lavish party can be underway

09:01.874 --> 09:03.876
while someone freezes to death
on the other.

09:05.378 --> 09:10.132
Is that why you used other people's money
to buy luxury goods and live lavishly?

09:10.216 --> 09:12.802
CHEONGDAM GODDESS RESALE SCAM
INVESTIGATION REPORT

09:14.303 --> 09:15.930
Oh, this case.

09:16.722 --> 09:18.641
Yes, I've heard of it before.

09:19.642 --> 09:20.977
But I remember hearing

09:21.477 --> 09:23.688
that the suspect committed suicide.

09:24.647 --> 09:25.982
So that's not you?

09:28.401 --> 09:29.860
I'm alive, aren't I?

09:35.700 --> 09:37.535
Then I wonder how this person

09:38.035 --> 09:42.248
wrote a Boudoir product review
before the brand even existed?

09:42.331 --> 09:43.583
Who knows?

09:44.417 --> 09:45.793
The dead tell no tales.

09:47.920 --> 09:53.259
But wasn't this case already closed
due to lack of prosecutorial authority?

09:54.135 --> 09:57.930
The suspect can't even be punished
unless she comes back to life.

09:58.723 --> 10:01.142
This isn't what's important, Detective.

10:01.642 --> 10:04.812
You haven't even come remotely close
to what I'm about to say.

10:06.439 --> 10:08.899
Luxury brands became luxury brands

10:09.400 --> 10:11.611
because they discarded what mattered most.

10:12.445 --> 10:13.321
Clients.

10:14.196 --> 10:17.074
The more you ignore them,
the more they want you.

10:17.575 --> 10:19.785
That attitude is what makes you
a luxury brand.

10:20.828 --> 10:22.955
Which is why I discarded myself.

10:24.206 --> 10:26.542
So that I could start over from scratch…

10:28.919 --> 10:30.921
in a place where no one asked my name.

10:39.930 --> 10:42.850
Fuck, this is why
I didn't want to be the first pick.

10:42.933 --> 10:45.061
He wouldn't keep
his fucking hands to himself.

10:45.144 --> 10:46.687
Hey, move.

10:56.781 --> 10:58.407
What are you glaring at?

11:01.619 --> 11:02.495
Well…

11:04.080 --> 11:06.123
I'm a follower of yours.

11:06.624 --> 11:09.543
I took your advice
and tried the eyelash extension place.

11:10.252 --> 11:12.171
- Really?
- Yes.

11:15.383 --> 11:16.258
I'll follow back.

11:26.852 --> 11:27.812
Here.

11:37.071 --> 11:39.156
How long have you been doing this job?

11:41.742 --> 11:43.327
This is just a temp gig for me.

11:43.411 --> 11:45.955
I'm quitting once I save enough
to start my business.

11:46.038 --> 11:46.997
"A temp gig"?

11:49.375 --> 11:51.877
It's temporary for you,
but it's a lifetime for me?

11:52.795 --> 11:53.713
So?

11:54.296 --> 11:55.798
How much have you saved up?

11:57.842 --> 11:59.885
Not that much.

12:01.011 --> 12:03.264
You didn't take
an upfront payment, did you?

12:07.810 --> 12:09.478
Idiot.

12:12.273 --> 12:14.859
Don't just look at how they spend money

12:14.942 --> 12:17.445
but at how they earn it.

12:19.780 --> 12:21.699
Like school, regional, and blood ties?

12:22.867 --> 12:25.327
But you can't have those things
even if you try.

12:27.747 --> 12:28.956
Of course you can.

12:30.040 --> 12:31.542
Just find yourself a sucker,

12:32.376 --> 12:34.420
and he'll get you a new identity.

12:37.465 --> 12:39.675
Is this a real diamond?

12:39.759 --> 12:41.135
Not a chance.

12:42.428 --> 12:45.306
But everyone will think it is
if I put it on you.

12:45.389 --> 12:48.476
I even sold my soul
just to get into that world.

12:48.559 --> 12:51.645
- I didn't realize the look until today.
- That's what I mean.

12:51.729 --> 12:55.441
I'm all dressed up too.
Look at Eun-jae. She's dressed so nicely.

12:55.524 --> 12:56.358
Honey, you're…

12:56.442 --> 12:59.445
The moment I entered that world,
I suddenly had some serious pull.

13:00.029 --> 13:01.322
Aren't you being too rash?

13:01.405 --> 13:03.073
The world was on my side.

13:03.574 --> 13:06.869
I just realized
everyone here went to Oxbridge.

13:07.870 --> 13:08.871
Oh, really?

13:08.954 --> 13:11.373
They say drinking makgeolli
on the campus lawn

13:11.457 --> 13:13.584
is a fond pastime of a Korean college.

13:13.667 --> 13:14.835
But for us,

13:14.919 --> 13:19.006
it was gulping down muddy water
when our punts capsized.

13:19.965 --> 13:23.427
These days, I do miss
the taste of that muddy water.

13:24.678 --> 13:26.639
I wondered when he'd bring that up.

13:27.139 --> 13:28.140
Seriously.

13:29.225 --> 13:32.603
Eun-jae, I take it
you've never gotten a failing grade?

13:35.439 --> 13:37.149
Oh, I guess I haven't--

13:37.233 --> 13:40.152
So, regarding the thing
you mentioned last time…

13:40.236 --> 13:41.987
He's no fun, is he?

13:44.073 --> 13:45.908
No, it's just that…

13:47.993 --> 13:50.496
I actually graduated
thanks to a ghostwritten thesis.

13:50.579 --> 13:52.373
My attendance was appalling too.

13:55.042 --> 13:57.294
You seem genuinely nice. No sneaky side.

13:58.045 --> 14:01.215
Let's meet up
without the husbands next time.

14:01.298 --> 14:03.175
I'll take you somewhere fun.

14:04.969 --> 14:06.011
Where?

14:08.013 --> 14:12.309
Somewhere with guys in a hot pool,
not those who gulp down muddy water.

14:13.018 --> 14:14.603
Isn't life ironic?

14:16.021 --> 14:18.274
I tried so hard to look like them…

14:18.357 --> 14:19.441
Shall we say…

14:19.525 --> 14:22.403
…but they make an effort
to look like who I used to be.

14:22.987 --> 14:27.658
It's like a web made strictly
by introductions between associates.

14:30.202 --> 14:32.746
- Is this your first?
- Yes.

14:33.581 --> 14:36.125
Being so young,
you must feel cooped up at home.

14:36.625 --> 14:38.711
Actually, I've been working
on a business idea

14:39.795 --> 14:41.463
to bring in a luxury brand here.

14:42.298 --> 14:44.466
But I don't know
the geography of Seoul well,

14:44.550 --> 14:46.886
so I'm not sure where to open the store.

14:46.969 --> 14:48.929
I have a building in Cheongdam.

14:49.013 --> 14:51.223
The location is good. Want to take a look?

14:51.307 --> 14:53.684
Yes, Chairwoman Jeong,
you should help her.

14:53.767 --> 14:55.477
I'll rent it to you cheap,

14:55.561 --> 14:58.606
and you can raise
the building's value for me, Eun-jae.

14:59.106 --> 15:01.692
For some reason,
every tenant goes bust and leaves.

15:01.775 --> 15:04.361
I know, right?
It's right in the main area too.

15:04.445 --> 15:06.280
145, CHEONGDAM-DONG, GANGNAM-GU, SEOUL

15:07.031 --> 15:08.449
It's in the luxury district.

15:12.202 --> 15:13.370
Hi.

15:13.454 --> 15:14.288
It's been a while.

15:14.371 --> 15:16.665
I'm not saying I'm entirely innocent here.

15:16.749 --> 15:19.460
But people pay money for fake degrees.

15:19.543 --> 15:21.587
I just made up credentials I never had.

15:22.087 --> 15:23.714
Who's more at fault?

15:23.797 --> 15:25.549
You never put in fair effort either.

15:26.467 --> 15:27.885
What about you, Detective?

15:27.968 --> 15:30.763
Are you being justly rewarded
for your fair efforts?

15:33.974 --> 15:35.976
Your watch doesn't suit today.

15:37.353 --> 15:38.312
Don't you have money?

15:40.064 --> 15:43.108
Or do you not care how others see you?

15:44.693 --> 15:45.861
If it's not that either,

15:45.945 --> 15:48.822
are you pretending not to care
what people think

15:48.906 --> 15:51.617
just to hide the fact
you can't afford an expensive watch?

15:51.700 --> 15:53.494
You've just admitted

15:54.328 --> 15:58.540
to posing as a Korean American
and falsifying academic credentials.

15:58.624 --> 15:59.458
Am I correct?

15:59.541 --> 16:01.210
Yes, I admit it.

16:02.544 --> 16:05.673
While I can be morally criticized
for impersonation,

16:05.756 --> 16:07.758
there's no actual law against it,
is there?

16:07.841 --> 16:10.135
And falsifying academic credentials
is just a fine

16:10.219 --> 16:11.929
unless I'm a high-ranking official.

16:12.429 --> 16:14.181
A fine of 80,000 won, right?

16:14.264 --> 16:18.060
If committed for financial gain,
the two charges constitute fraud.

16:18.143 --> 16:21.105
A 50 billion won fraud is punishable
by severe penalties.

16:21.188 --> 16:22.856
That's a bit of a stretch.

16:23.565 --> 16:26.735
Who cares about a seller's education
and background when buying a bag?

16:26.819 --> 16:29.405
You swindled 15 billion won from Jeong
for investment.

16:30.447 --> 16:33.826
Jeong handed over the funds
before Boudoir had officially launched.

16:33.909 --> 16:37.121
The timing suggests
it wasn't the brand she invested in

16:37.204 --> 16:40.666
but you, with your fake background
and education. Is that a stretch?

16:41.709 --> 16:44.503
When Jeong Yeo-jin was arrested
for embezzlement,

16:45.004 --> 16:47.006
it seems
you wanted to cover it up somehow.

16:47.506 --> 16:49.299
You rushed to repay the full amount.

16:50.509 --> 16:51.802
I think you have it wrong.

16:51.885 --> 16:54.013
All transactions have been confirmed.

16:54.096 --> 16:57.182
No, those were dividends,
not repayment of the investment.

16:58.350 --> 17:00.644
If you recover your principal
in less than a year,

17:00.728 --> 17:02.688
don't you think
that's a decent investment?

17:03.897 --> 17:06.567
It may begin with a bluff,
but if it ends with success,

17:07.443 --> 17:09.361
it's business, not a con.

17:11.447 --> 17:12.448
I'll say this again.

17:13.365 --> 17:16.326
I didn't create Boudoir to deceive anyone.

17:17.161 --> 17:19.079
I built Boudoir

17:19.580 --> 17:20.998
so I wouldn't have to do that.

17:26.670 --> 17:29.298
The Boudoir appraisal report
has arrived, sir.

17:30.799 --> 17:33.761
I'm sure you know
exactly what it says, right?

17:34.595 --> 17:37.431
You sold bags worth just 180,000 won
for millions,

17:38.140 --> 17:40.642
tens of millions,
even hundreds of millions of won.

17:42.102 --> 17:45.105
Production costs do not determine
the value of luxury goods.

17:45.939 --> 17:49.693
People chase the status that comes
with the brand, not the product itself.

17:50.235 --> 17:53.238
"I like the brand's heritage."
"I like its identity."

17:53.322 --> 17:54.406
That's all bullshit.

17:55.491 --> 17:57.826
I sold the added value of superiority

17:57.910 --> 18:00.579
and set a reasonable price accordingly.

18:13.425 --> 18:16.678
She's admitting to the charges
while dodging punishment.

18:18.472 --> 18:19.848
It's flawed logic,

18:20.724 --> 18:21.809
but it makes sense.

18:22.976 --> 18:23.977
How is this possible?

18:24.478 --> 18:25.646
Tell me about it.

18:25.729 --> 18:27.689
He has been outmaneuvered too.

18:28.190 --> 18:31.193
No, he's waiting
for the contradiction to peak.

18:31.693 --> 18:33.028
Let's get Financial Crimes.

18:33.529 --> 18:35.239
JEONG YEO-JIN

18:35.322 --> 18:38.659
Would people still have bought them
if they had known the production cost?

18:39.243 --> 18:43.664
Everyone knows that luxury goods
are expensive because of the brand value.

18:43.747 --> 18:45.916
What if they knew
the bags were made in Korea?

18:49.837 --> 18:53.090
This is the import declaration document
seized from the Boudoir store.

18:53.173 --> 18:54.842
With this one forged document,

18:54.925 --> 18:58.262
you turned bags made in Sinwol-dong
into "Made in the UK."

18:58.345 --> 19:00.597
Yes, the bags were manufactured
in Sinwol-dong.

19:01.098 --> 19:03.100
But that document is not forged.

19:04.893 --> 19:07.271
The bags were produced
with the top handles detached

19:07.354 --> 19:08.689
then sent to the UK.

19:09.565 --> 19:11.567
Once there, they were reassembled,

19:12.067 --> 19:14.570
then reimported to Korea
to get the document.

19:14.653 --> 19:15.779
Legally.

19:39.469 --> 19:41.638
That can't be called legal.
You used a loophole.

19:42.181 --> 19:44.892
You could say I did,
but it's also not illegal.

19:45.601 --> 19:49.521
Do you know how far I went
to make Boudoir a luxury brand?

19:50.147 --> 19:52.983
I deliberately made
and distributed counterfeits.

19:53.066 --> 19:55.110
No counterfeits exist
without luxury goods.

19:55.194 --> 19:59.156
On the flip side, if counterfeits exist,
it must be a luxury brand.

20:57.923 --> 21:00.509
So if I'm a fraud,
then every other brand is too.

21:01.176 --> 21:02.886
And as long as they're not frauds,

21:03.553 --> 21:05.055
I'm not one either.

21:06.848 --> 21:09.226
Do you understand
what Boudoir means to me…

21:11.228 --> 21:14.231
and what it is you're messing with?

21:16.066 --> 21:17.651
Do you get it now?

21:19.361 --> 21:22.322
I will do anything to protect Boudoir.

21:23.323 --> 21:25.158
Damn.

21:26.910 --> 21:29.371
Proving trademark infringement
won't be easy either.

21:29.454 --> 21:30.831
I know.

21:31.999 --> 21:36.128
Is that why you stole the heritage
of a luxury brand?

21:36.920 --> 21:39.589
"Crafted for European royalty
for 100 years."

21:39.673 --> 21:41.717
"A British Royal Warrant Holder."

21:41.800 --> 21:45.429
How do you justify promoting the brand
with a history that doesn't exist?

21:47.681 --> 21:49.266
It wasn't exactly promotion.

21:49.766 --> 21:51.435
It was just word of mouth, I think.

21:52.060 --> 21:52.894
Pass them down.

21:52.978 --> 21:54.187
God is in the details.

21:54.271 --> 21:55.605
- "Bu-do-ire"?
- What's this?

21:55.689 --> 21:56.523
"Bu-do-ire."

21:56.606 --> 21:58.108
First time seeing this, right?

21:58.734 --> 22:00.110
Hey, open it carefully.

22:00.193 --> 22:01.361
And this money here…

22:01.445 --> 22:02.446
This one's mine.

22:02.529 --> 22:04.239
This is for promoting. Get on it.

22:04.323 --> 22:05.324
Thank you.

22:05.407 --> 22:07.117
Details amass to build credibility.

22:11.830 --> 22:12.664
Hey.

22:13.206 --> 22:14.708
You should get a new bag.

22:16.043 --> 22:18.170
Why? Does it look weird?

22:19.046 --> 22:20.589
No, it's just that

22:20.672 --> 22:24.301
all the ministers' wives in the next room
couldn't stop talking about Boudoir.

22:24.384 --> 22:28.347
They say these days, owning a Boudoir bag
is a sign of true wealth.

22:30.474 --> 22:31.308
Hey.

22:31.391 --> 22:32.225
Yes.

22:33.310 --> 22:35.437
Credibility builds into trust.

22:40.108 --> 22:42.527
And when trust grows, it becomes faith.

22:43.362 --> 22:45.447
But I played absolutely no part in that.

22:46.114 --> 22:48.075
So if I'm a con artist,

22:49.576 --> 22:51.870
that would make them accomplices,
not victims.

22:51.953 --> 22:54.581
Would you be able to stand
in front of the victims

22:54.664 --> 22:56.291
and call them accomplices?

22:56.375 --> 22:57.876
There's no reason I can't.

22:58.627 --> 22:59.920
But…

23:01.088 --> 23:05.342
has even a single victim come forward
to formally accuse me of fraud?

23:07.219 --> 23:09.471
Have you met the purchasers?

23:10.013 --> 23:11.932
Were they willing to make statements?

23:14.434 --> 23:17.646
They spend hundreds of millions of won
on a bag for social status.

23:18.730 --> 23:21.400
I wonder if they'd come forward
as fraud victims.

23:28.448 --> 23:30.075
What I'm saying is…

23:32.577 --> 23:34.079
there are no victims.

23:34.746 --> 23:36.331
So how is this a con?

23:37.374 --> 23:38.959
This case

23:39.459 --> 23:43.338
can't even be established
in the first place.

23:51.930 --> 23:53.432
Let's take a short break.

23:57.644 --> 23:58.603
Now.

24:28.049 --> 24:28.884
Goodness.

24:29.384 --> 24:30.886
You should've just died.

24:30.969 --> 24:33.096
Why are you still alive? Why?

24:33.180 --> 24:34.806
What do you think you're doing?

24:34.890 --> 24:36.266
Hurry up and go inside.

24:36.349 --> 24:38.477
What the hell did you do?

24:38.977 --> 24:39.978
Hey!

24:40.061 --> 24:41.646
INTERROGATION IN PROGRESS

24:46.985 --> 24:49.362
Jeong Yeo-jin said
nothing about being defrauded

24:49.446 --> 24:51.490
because she believed Sarah Kim was dead.

24:52.532 --> 24:55.368
Now that she's seen Kim alive,
she might decide

24:55.869 --> 24:57.579
to take her down with her.

24:57.662 --> 25:00.457
Her resentment runs deep enough
to spit at a corpse.

25:01.166 --> 25:02.918
Let's hope we can count on that.

25:20.185 --> 25:23.855
I'm sure I don't need to explain
why we're having this confrontation.

25:24.481 --> 25:27.400
Ms. Jeong, you're undergoing
a custodial investigation,

25:27.484 --> 25:29.277
suspected of embezzling 15 billion won.

25:29.361 --> 25:32.572
I did not embezzle.
I was making an investment.

25:34.199 --> 25:35.283
It doesn't matter.

25:35.367 --> 25:37.786
We're not here
to interrogate you, Ms. Jeong,

25:38.578 --> 25:40.747
but to prove the crimes of this suspect.

25:41.623 --> 25:44.167
Ms. Jeong, in your previous interview,

25:44.251 --> 25:47.379
you said you invested 15 billion won
with Sarah Kim

25:47.462 --> 25:49.798
after she told you about Hotel Boudoir.

25:49.881 --> 25:50.966
Is that correct?

25:51.925 --> 25:53.218
I don't recall.

25:54.261 --> 25:56.471
I was not in my right mind then,

25:57.430 --> 25:59.391
having lost a close friend.

26:02.018 --> 26:03.061
Ms. Jeong Yeo-jin.

26:04.187 --> 26:06.147
Did you say "a close friend"?

26:06.856 --> 26:09.859
Do you know her real name?
Her age? Where she went to school?

26:09.943 --> 26:10.902
Anything?

26:12.487 --> 26:13.697
"A close friend"?

26:15.198 --> 26:16.533
Will you fall for it again?

26:17.325 --> 26:18.952
Think carefully.

26:20.662 --> 26:22.539
Everything about her was a lie.

26:23.415 --> 26:26.710
Do you think she was ever honest with you,
even for a moment?

26:30.797 --> 26:32.465
The suspect is denying

26:32.549 --> 26:36.720
all charges against her,
as no one has filed a formal complaint.

26:38.138 --> 26:39.222
No one?

26:40.932 --> 26:42.142
Yes. At this rate,

26:42.642 --> 26:45.604
proving the allegations,
let alone punishment, may be difficult.

26:48.898 --> 26:50.942
I have suffered no damages.

26:53.653 --> 26:55.530
Don't you realize the consequences

26:56.865 --> 26:59.075
of the statement you've just made?

27:00.160 --> 27:03.330
Would you be okay
with the suspect's crimes being dismissed?

27:05.165 --> 27:07.250
If Boudoir turns out not to be a scam,

27:08.543 --> 27:11.546
then what Jeong did
isn't embezzlement either, right?

27:14.299 --> 27:15.133
That's right.

27:21.681 --> 27:23.433
Do you know what you're throwing away

27:24.809 --> 27:26.269
and what you're protecting?

27:29.356 --> 27:31.608
I have not thrown anything away.

27:34.903 --> 27:36.363
I have no objections.

27:39.199 --> 27:40.450
Are we done?

27:41.910 --> 27:43.411
Am I free to go?

27:49.209 --> 27:51.211
Go and get Jeong Yeo-jin out.

28:25.620 --> 28:28.039
I was considering suing you
for defamation…

28:30.041 --> 28:31.334
but I won't do that.

28:31.418 --> 28:33.336
You seem to be suffering enough already.

28:36.381 --> 28:37.215
Seriously…

28:37.799 --> 28:39.676
You stupid bastard.

28:41.219 --> 28:42.470
I'm sorry, sir.

28:42.554 --> 28:44.264
I wasn't talking to you.

28:45.223 --> 28:46.641
I was talking to myself.

28:47.976 --> 28:50.603
Chances should be given
to people who know how to use them.

28:52.313 --> 28:53.773
I made a mistake.

28:55.859 --> 29:02.490
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY
REGIONAL INVESTIGATION DIVISION

29:24.971 --> 29:28.224
It was wrong of me
to even want to become rich.

29:29.434 --> 29:32.479
You don't become rich.
You're born that way.

29:34.022 --> 29:36.441
It was wrong of me
to have been born this way.

29:37.442 --> 29:39.235
I was born the wrong way.

29:39.736 --> 29:41.863
Let me help you sign up
for membership first.

29:41.946 --> 29:43.281
May I have your name, please?

29:47.869 --> 29:49.204
Sarah.

29:51.080 --> 29:52.248
Sarah Kim.

30:17.148 --> 30:18.983
Please help those in need.

30:19.692 --> 30:20.693
SALVATION ARMY

30:20.777 --> 30:21.986
Please help those in need.

30:24.113 --> 30:26.032
Let us share our warmth.

30:38.378 --> 30:42.090
We have set up a collection kettle
to help those around us in need.

30:45.718 --> 30:46.803
RED KETTLE

30:47.303 --> 30:48.972
Please help those in need.

30:53.852 --> 30:56.229
What the… She's giving all that?

30:58.022 --> 31:00.775
Thank you.

31:00.859 --> 31:02.819
Yes, over here.

31:02.902 --> 31:04.237
We have it in red.

31:04.737 --> 31:08.366
How do you like this model?
The sexy vibe suits you very well.

31:09.617 --> 31:12.036
Are you looking for a long-term rental?

31:12.912 --> 31:14.455
No, just one day.

31:15.373 --> 31:17.375
Then how about this one?

31:17.458 --> 31:19.544
If you roll down the window, the side is…

31:20.420 --> 31:22.088
Just insanely beautiful.

31:23.923 --> 31:25.758
Do you have a specific car in mind?

31:28.595 --> 31:30.013
A Rolls-Royce.

31:31.598 --> 31:32.682
This one.

31:32.765 --> 31:35.476
This is a Rolls-Royce.

31:36.060 --> 31:36.895
Here.

32:06.174 --> 32:08.551
- Just leave it, please.
- Yes, ma'am.

32:11.095 --> 32:12.805
We wish you a pleasant day.

32:14.515 --> 32:15.767
Just a moment.

32:29.155 --> 32:29.989
Thank you.

32:46.839 --> 32:47.674
APOLOGY

32:47.757 --> 32:48.758
CHEONGDAM GODDESS HERE

32:48.841 --> 32:51.094
I CAN'T SHIP ITEMS
DUE TO UNFORESEEN CIRCUMSTANCES

32:51.177 --> 32:52.011
I'M SORRY

33:10.029 --> 33:12.323
I wish I could be born again.

33:38.391 --> 33:40.768
I'm here to stay for good.

33:41.644 --> 33:43.021
You know, I have a dream now.

33:43.688 --> 33:45.606
I want to become a person
who suits this bag.

35:18.783 --> 35:19.784
EDIT

35:40.179 --> 35:43.015
I GOT THE LUXURY BOUDOIR BAG LOVED
BY EUROPEAN ROYALS FOR 100 YEARS

35:50.648 --> 35:53.151
The world is kind yet indifferent.

35:54.652 --> 35:57.155
On one side,
a lavish party can be underway

35:57.738 --> 35:59.824
while someone freezes to death
on the other.

36:03.369 --> 36:04.287
Stop there!

36:06.706 --> 36:07.832
- Play it back.
- Sir?

36:07.915 --> 36:09.458
- I said play it back.
- Yes, sir.

36:13.296 --> 36:15.882
The world is kind yet indifferent.

36:17.049 --> 36:19.260
On one side,
a lavish party can be underway

36:19.844 --> 36:21.929
while someone freezes to death
on the other.

36:23.848 --> 36:24.891
Get her.

36:24.974 --> 36:25.808
Yes, sir.

36:44.076 --> 36:45.953
Do we still have something to discuss?

36:46.037 --> 36:50.917
You are under arrest without a warrant
for the Jane Doe sewer murder.

37:00.426 --> 37:04.013
You have the right to an attorney
and the right not to incriminate yourself.

37:04.096 --> 37:06.182
You will have the chance
to explain yourself

37:07.850 --> 37:10.519
and the right to request
a detention review from the court.

37:10.603 --> 37:13.648
Why are you so set on arresting me?

37:22.823 --> 37:26.035
On what grounds are you accusing me
of being a murderer this time?

37:28.371 --> 37:30.289
The Jane Doe sewer murder case.

37:31.249 --> 37:36.254
As it happens, the murder occurred
on the same night as your Boudoir party.

37:38.673 --> 37:40.633
Then you must already know.

37:41.217 --> 37:43.177
My alibi for that day is overwhelming.

37:47.515 --> 37:49.809
The world is kind yet indifferent.

37:50.393 --> 37:52.770
On one side,
a lavish party can be underway

37:53.271 --> 37:55.314
while someone freezes to death
on the other.

37:55.815 --> 37:59.151
You let something only the suspect
and the police know slip.

37:59.986 --> 38:03.572
It was never made public
that the victim froze to death.

38:05.241 --> 38:07.076
And based on that statement,

38:07.576 --> 38:12.331
you have become the last person
to see the victim alive

38:12.415 --> 38:14.917
and the only suspect
who knows the cause of death.

38:20.339 --> 38:23.551
If you had taken the entire 50 billion won
and disappeared,

38:24.093 --> 38:26.721
I would've thought
it was a meticulously planned murder.

38:27.388 --> 38:29.098
But you didn't do that.

38:30.308 --> 38:32.393
Something happened that day, didn't it?

38:36.522 --> 38:38.983
Accidental killings
can be a mitigating factor.

38:43.154 --> 38:44.864
Was it premeditated?

38:44.947 --> 38:45.865
Or were you

38:46.615 --> 38:48.200
acting on impulse?

38:52.246 --> 38:54.457
Could I have a cigarette?

38:55.082 --> 38:56.375
We've got her.

38:57.335 --> 38:59.795
Whether she calls it
premeditated or impulsive,

39:00.296 --> 39:02.715
she's finally admitting
she committed the murder.

39:06.344 --> 39:08.846
God, I tried so hard to quit these things.

39:11.474 --> 39:12.767
Did you know?

39:14.435 --> 39:17.646
Every single wealthy person I met
quit smoking

39:18.314 --> 39:19.940
so they could live longer.

39:21.859 --> 39:24.278
Detective, have you ever thought,

39:24.362 --> 39:26.447
"I want to live just a day longer"?

39:29.617 --> 39:32.078
No matter how desperately
I tried to be like them,

39:33.746 --> 39:36.707
I couldn't even bring myself
to think something like that.

40:25.631 --> 40:28.175
Have I become like this
because I lived tirelessly?

40:29.677 --> 40:32.263
Or did I live tirelessly
to become like this?

40:32.763 --> 40:34.056
Detective.

40:34.598 --> 40:36.642
The reason people trusted me

40:37.143 --> 40:40.062
isn't because I had some special skill.

40:41.981 --> 40:43.274
I just knew

40:44.692 --> 40:47.278
what they desperately wanted.

40:48.446 --> 40:50.656
And it appears
you want something from me too.

40:52.158 --> 40:54.285
You're desperate for my confession.

41:02.293 --> 41:03.419
Detective.

41:03.502 --> 41:06.130
I did some research before coming here.

41:07.298 --> 41:12.386
"The arrest warrant must be requested
within 48 hours of arresting the suspect."

41:12.470 --> 41:17.600
"If the warrant is not requested
or is not issued within 48 hours,

41:17.683 --> 41:20.478
the suspect must be immediately released."

41:21.353 --> 41:22.605
What comes next?

41:24.273 --> 41:25.107
That's right.

41:26.901 --> 41:29.069
"A person released under this regulation

41:29.153 --> 41:34.033
cannot be rearrested for the same crime
without a warrant."

41:35.409 --> 41:38.370
If I run, I'm a con artist.
Arrested, I'm a murderer.

41:40.039 --> 41:41.957
But if I get released from here,

41:42.708 --> 41:44.543
what would people call me?

41:50.633 --> 41:52.635
You have 47 hours left now.

42:06.357 --> 42:09.485
WARRANT REQUEST DEADLINE

43:34.570 --> 43:39.575
Subtitle translation by: Yung Un Choi
